  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. It replaces a record naming the owner as reviewer, because that record's fingerprint no longer matched; that record stays in git history. Read proxy.aws_kms_adapter, proxy.gcp_kms_adapter and proxy.pkcs11_adapter against their diffs since 2026-10-14. PKCS#11: pkcs11_native.rs became pkcs11_native/{closer,ec_point,error,find_objects,identity,session,session_ref,sign,template}.rs. I compared every function old to new: sign_eddsa and get_ec_point have identical bodies with self.function_list and self.handle in place of the passed values (same length-query, MAX_SIGNATURE_LEN and MAX_EC_POINT_LEN refusals, same written-length check); find_objects keeps init, collect, finalize in the same order, and its paging loop (PAGE 16, found greater than PAGE refused, MAX_OBJECT_HANDLES refused, stop on a short page) is the same logic as three small functions; the remaining functions are unchanged lines. pkcs11_keysource/ has no diff, and the e2e test changed only its ServerOptions constructor argument. AWS KMS: aws_kms_keysource.rs changed only the HTTP call chain (ureq 3 through outbound_fetch: header, bounded_by(NETWORK_TIMEOUT), fetch_with; Failure::Status) and the Presentation argument to recover; read_kms_response keeps its 256 KiB cap and bounded error body, and the credential_refusal split into suspension.rs keeps the same retry predicate order (refused, not suspended, then invalidate), the same cool-off arithmetic and the same clear-on-success; the tests that changed moved a helper without changing an expectation. GCP KMS: gcp_kms_keysource.rs changed only the same call chain and read_body type. The advertised-key establishment, the Ed25519-only algorithm refusal, the destroyed-key-version refusal, the SPKI check, verify-before-return and construction-time endpoint refusal are unchanged lines in all three adapters. The endpoint is still reached through CredentialEgress, whose agent disables redirects (max_redirects(0)). All 18 tested symbols per unit still resolve by name. Dependencies THM-0108 and THM-0089 are REVIEWED. The claim holds. The three feature lanes and the mutation lane were not run. Evidence class as registered (V0, software-protection custody; no FIPS claim).",
